---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import Draft from '../../components/Draft.astro';
import Provider from '../../components/Provider.astro';
import { entity } from '../../lib/entity';
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Imprint', description: 'Who runs version.cam, and how to reach them.' }}>
	<Draft />
	<p class="vc-lead">
		version.cam is run by a Slovenian sole proprietorship. Slovenian law (ZEPT, Article 5) asks a provider of an
		information-society service to keep these facts easy to find, so here they are, on one page, linked from every
		other.
	</p>
	<Provider />

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		For anything, <a href={`mailto:${entity.contactEmail}`}>{entity.contactEmail}</a>: a question, a bill, a
		request about your personal data (the <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy page</a> says what you can ask for), or
		a clip you believe should not be hosted (the <a href="/legal/terms/#reporting">terms</a> say what to send and
		what happens next). A security vulnerability goes to the address in
		<a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>, which is the same one. We answer in English or Slovene.
	</p>

	<h2>Supervisory authority for data protection</h2>
	<p>
		Informacijski pooblaščenec Republike Slovenije, the Information Commissioner: Dunajska cesta 22, 1000 Ljubljana,
		Slovenia; <a href="https://www.ip-rs.si/">ip-rs.si</a>; gp.ip@ip-rs.si. You may complain there about how we
		handle your personal data, or to the authority where you live.
	</p>

	<h2>Point of contact under the Digital Services Act</h2>
	<p>
		clips.version.cam stores the clips our customers publish and serves them to the public, which makes version.cam
		a hosting service under Regulation (EU) 2022/2065. The single point of contact for the authorities of the Member
		States, the European Commission and the Board (Article 11), and for anyone who uses the service (Article 12),
		is <a href={`mailto:${entity.contactEmail}`}>{entity.contactEmail}</a>, in English or Slovene. As a
		micro-enterprise, version.cam is exempt from the Act's duties for online platforms and from its transparency
		reports (Articles 15(2) and 19). What applies is this point of contact, terms that say what may not be hosted,
		a way to report content you believe is illegal, and a reason when something is removed; the
		<a href="/legal/terms/#reporting">terms</a> hold the last three.
	</p>

	<h2>The brand and the firma</h2>
	<p>
		Versioncam and version.cam are the names of the product and the site. The legal person behind them is the one
		named above: a contract, an invoice or a notice names it, never the brand.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>
